      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name}I'm not sure, \"You have been kicked by person X\" would be the obvious solution, but I can also see the problem with that. Maybe being in a group instance should show the list of avatars in that instance with moderator powers? It wouldn't necessarily tell you who kicked someone, but you would at least be aware of who is \"managing\" that instance and whether they might have a problem with you.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-01-01T07:11:07.842Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If you get kicked from a regular instance, it is safe to say that it was either through a vote, or that the instance owner or world owner kicked you personally. On group instances however, as a non group member, or a basic member, you can't see roles, their members, or their powers.\n\nThis creates this weird situation where group instances are a bit of a black box, you don't know who is running the place, who started the instance, if there is a moderator in the instance, why you were kicked out, by whom, or who to contact about it.",
